{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RevocationFeed"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"What this narrows, and what it is not","anchor":"What-this-narrows-and-what-it-is-not"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An AXIAM access token is self-contained and valid for up to fifteen minutes, and this SDK","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verifies it locally. A logout, a role removal or an account disable therefore does not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reach a token already in a caller’s hands until it expires — §10.2 records that, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"documented answer has been “route the decision through gRPC introspection instead”, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is correct and costs a round trip ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"per request"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A deployment may publish ","type":"text"},{"code":"GET \/oauth2\/revocations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the base64url-unpadded SHA-256 of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every session id revoked within the last access-token lifetime. A guard that polls it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rejects a revoked session within ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"one poll interval","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" instead of one token lifetime, for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one cacheable fetch per interval.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It is NOT a control, and every rule below follows from that:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Default off."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Nothing polls unless a caller constructs one and attaches it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Never on the request path."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/isRevoked(_:)"},{"text":" answers from the cached set and, at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most, refreshes a set the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"next"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" caller sees.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Never fail closed."}]},{"type":"text","text":" An unreachable feed, a non-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"200"},{"type":"text","text":", a body that does not parse, an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alg"},{"type":"text","text":" this build does not know — every one of them behaves exactly as no feed at all."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Not as an empty list: an empty list asserts that nothing has been revoked, which is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guard that silently honours no revocations while appearing to honour them."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"It only ever rejects.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every §10.1 rule runs first and still decides. The feed can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn an accept into a reject and never the reverse."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A token with no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sid"},{"type":"text","text":" is never matched."}]},{"type":"text","text":" There is no session behind a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"client-credentials token, an RPT or a token exchange, and hashing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jti"},{"type":"text","text":" instead would"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match nothing while looking like it worked."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actor"},{"type":"text","text":", so one instance can be shared across guards and they poll once between them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than once each. Callers do not build one directly: set"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamConfig\/revocationFeedEnabled"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/AxiamClient"},{"type":"text","text":" wires it to the same transport"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every other call already uses."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The optional session-revocation feed poller (CONTRACT.md §10.4, contract 1.44 — AXIAM","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"threats T-39 and T-143).","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/effectivePollInterval","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/feedURL"],"title":"Instance Properties"},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/isRevoked(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/RevocationFeed\/refresh()"],"title":"Instance Methods"},{